# ==========================================================================
# MMM-MASTERY .gitignore
#
# Governing rules:
#   MMM_MASTER_STUDENT_RESEARCH_AGENT.md §9
#   README.md §13
#
# Two priorities:
#   1. Never commit proprietary bootcamp source media.
#   2. Never commit secrets.
# ==========================================================================

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOURCE VIDEOS — proprietary course material, large binaries.
# Represented in Git only by 00_SYSTEM/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md (name + size +
# duration + SHA-256 + path). Never modify the originals.
# Committing these would require an explicit decision in DECISIONS.md and
# Git LFS — not normal Git history.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
01_SOURCE_VIDEOS/**
!01_SOURCE_VIDEOS/README.md
!01_SOURCE_VIDEOS/.gitkeep

# Video / audio formats anywhere in the tree
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.wmv
*.flv
*.webm
*.mpg
*.mpeg
# *.ts below = MPEG transport stream. NOTE: the pattern also matches TypeScript —
# if TS tooling is ever added to this project, narrow it to 01_SOURCE_VIDEOS/**/*.ts
*.ts
*.vob
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS AND CREDENTIALS — never commit
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
credentials/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
*.token
*_token
*_secret
*credentials*.json
.netrc
.htpasswd
broker_config.json
mt4_config.ini
mt5_config.ini
api_keys.*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / EDITOR NOISE
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPORARY / GENERATED
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
.cache/

# NOTE: *.log above is deliberate for stray tool logs, but the project journal
# LOG.md is a tracked Markdown file and is unaffected (different extension).

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON (validation / analysis tooling)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE (only if tooling is ever added)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LARGE DATA — market data used for manual/automated backtesting.
# Keep raw price dumps local; record their provenance in
# 06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/ documentation and in DECISIONS.md.
# Small, intentional CSV samples can be force-added with `git add -f`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/**
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/README.md
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/.gitkeep

# PROVENANCE IS NOT BULK DATA — a hash manifest is the audit trail, not the
# payload, and belongs in history. The `**` above swallowed it, which is why
# `D-036a` cited `datasets/HISTDATA_GBPUSD_M1/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt` as the
# integrity record for a corpus while that file existed only on the machine
# that built it. A checksum nobody else holds cannot verify anything. The rule
# was the defect; the file was there all along and its four hashes verify
# against the on-disk corpus. Un-ignored and committed 2026-08-14.
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/raw/
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/derived/
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/derived/SHA256SUMS.txt
# `D-044` adds a second derived set and a second QA gate. Same principle: the
# manifests and the gate reports are the audit trail. `QA_REPORT_EXT_RAW.txt` is
# committed FAILING on purpose — it is the record of what the vendor served, and
# a defect that is only ever seen in its repaired form is not on the record.
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/derived_ext/
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/derived_ext/SHA256SUMS.txt
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/QA_REPORT.txt
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/QA_REPORT_EXT.txt
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/QA_REPORT_EXT_RAW.txt

# Same principle, one directory up: a vendor-availability finding is documentation
# about where data can come from, not the data. Un-ignored 2026-08-14.
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/HISTDATA_RECENCY_CHECK.md

# The M15/H1 derivation (`feature/m15-h1-chart-backtest`, merged 2026-08-14)
# widens the same rule rather than restating it: a per-dataset `README.md` and
# the prose findings beside it are documentation about the corpus, and its QA
# gate ships more report names than the three enumerated above. The globs below
# subsume those explicit lines; the explicit lines are kept because the comment
# on `QA_REPORT_EXT_RAW.txt` is load-bearing and would otherwise lose its anchor.
# NOTE: that branch's own comment here claimed the M1 manifest "is in no branch
# of this repository". That was true when it was written and is FALSE now —
# `b97fa63` committed it. The HEAD prose above is the accurate record.
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/README.md
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/*.md
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/QA_REPORT*.txt
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/*/CROSSCHECK_REPORT.txt
# ...but never the bars themselves.
06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/datasets/**/*.csv

*.parquet
*.feather
*.sqlite
*.db

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RENDERED STUDY CHARTS — bulk output of 06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/tools/
# mmm_chart_render.py. Regenerate them from the committed script and the
# checksummed CSVs rather than carrying hundreds of PNGs in history. A small
# committed sample under `samples/` exists so a reviewer can see what the tool
# produces without running it.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/tools/chart_renders/**
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/tools/chart_renders/samples/
!06_MANUAL_BACKTEST/tools/chart_renders/samples/**

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTENTIONALLY TRACKED
#
# Screenshots (04_SCREENSHOTS/, 09_CHART_EXAMPLES/) are first-class evidence
# and ARE committed. Keep them reasonably sized — prefer PNG at readable but
# not excessive resolution. If the repository ever grows unwieldy, revisit
# with an explicit decision in DECISIONS.md rather than deleting evidence.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
